From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: association queries and handlers, shell data objects, active desktop wallpaper (3684)

shell32: association queries and handlers, shell data objects, active desktop wallpaper

QueryAppIsDefault and QueryAppIsDefaultAll compare the application's
declared ProgId (RegisteredApplications > Capabilities) with the default
at the level asked for (user choice, machine class default, effective), for
file extensions, URL protocols, MIME types and start menu clients;
ClearUserAssociations removes the UserChoice keys. SHAssocEnumHandlers
lists the programs that open a file type (recommended: what opens it now,
OpenWithProgids/OpenWithList, SupportedTypes) as IAssocHandler objects
(names, icon, IsRecommended, MakeDefault, Invoke, CreateInvoker), and
SHAssocEnumHandlersForProtocolByApplication the applications that declare a
protocol. SHCreateDataObject builds the shell data object (with an inner
object supplying other formats; absolute ids when no folder is given); the
shell data object now answers GetDataHere, GetCanonicalFormatEtc and the
advise calls (OLE_E_ADVISENOTSUPPORTED). SHGetDataFromIDList answers
SHGDFIL_DESCRIPTIONID. IEnumIDList::Clone. IActiveDesktop wallpaper,
wallpaper options, pattern, ApplyChanges, item count and item options.
DriveType, InvalidateDriveType, SHFlushClipboard, PathIsTemporaryW,
RegisterShellHook, SHRunControlPanel, SHStartNetConnectionDialog.
